      "writtenOn": "2026-11-15T05:07:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that keying refs by Change-Id is the proper long-term fix, but it\u0027s a NoteDb schema redesign (URLs, REST, events, download commands, Move renaming all refs, branch-name D/F conflicts like `a` vs `a/b`), which needs a design doc and can\u0027t go to stable branches.\n\nOn the cost of a reservation ref: it isn\u0027t doubling. Each change already has a meta ref plus one per patch set. On our largest repo there are 438k refs for 80k changes (4.2 refs per change under refs/changes, plus 100k tags), so one more ref per change is +18%. And it\u0027s only deleted on change deletion or Move, both rare; a regular push never deletes it.\n\nIf that\u0027s still not acceptable, I\u0027ll abandon this change and leave the issue open for the schema redesign.",
